igh","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-27","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: During a DFPS investigation there was sufficient evidence to support that an infant was able to climb out of a highchair and hit their head on the floor. One caregiver walked away from the infant sitting in the highchair, had their back towards the infant, and was using their personal cell phone. The other caregiver was facing the infant while sitting on the carpet and failed to get up and stand in front of the highchair knowing the infant has attempted to get out of the highchair previously.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026675017","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1351534-i20240712-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1203-3-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1351534-i20240712","date":"2024-07-12","original_code":"746.1203(3)(D)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-27","finding":"Personal use of electronic devices, such as cell phones, MP3 players, tablets, and video games: Information obtained throughout the investigation shows that caregivers use their personal cell phones while supervising children.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026666426","violation_type_title":"Personal use of electronic devices, such as cell phones, MP3 players, tablets, and video games (26 TAC §746.1203(3)(D))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1351534-i20240712-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-707","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1351534-i20240712","date":"2024-07-12","original_code":"746.707",